    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Baltic duchy on the lower Oder ruled by the Slavic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffin dynasty</a> from the 1120s until 1637.</li><li>Converted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-of-bamberg">Otto of Bamberg</a>, it became an imperial fief and absorbed German settlers and Hanseatic towns.</li><li>When the last duke died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years’ War, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> divided the duchy in 1648.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffin</a> prince, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-of-pomerania">Eric of Pomerania</a>, became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in 1397, and later ended his days as a minor duke in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

