n></li><li><span class="rf-year">1295</span><span class="rf-text">The duchy is divided into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-stettin">Pomerania-Stettin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-wolgast">Pomerania-Wolgast</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1478</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogislaw-x">Bogislaw X</a> reunites all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1534</span><span class="rf-text">A diet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trzebiatow">Treptow</a> adopts the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Lutheran Reformation</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1637</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogislaw-xiv">Bogislaw XIV</a> dies, the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffin</a> duke</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1648</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> divides <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a></span></li></ol>
